  {
   "id": "ex2",
   "type": "example",
   "problem": {
    "en": "If x + iy = (a + ib)/(a − ib), prove that x² + y² = 1."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "Take modulus: |x + iy| = |a + ib|/|a − ib|."
    },
    {
     "en": "|a + ib| = |a − ib| = √(a² + b²), so the ratio is 1."
    },
    {
     "en": "So √(x² + y²) = 1, that is x² + y² = 1."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "Proved"
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us solve this together. If x + iy = (a + ib)/(a − ib), prove that x² + y² = 1."
   }
